cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "bulkdeconv: Cell-Type Deconvolution of Tumor Bulk RNA-Seq Through One Function"
authors:
  - family-names: Kumakura
    given-names: Daiki
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9859-0720"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-12"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.24210482"
    description: "Archived release (Zenodo)"
repository-code: "https://github.com/DaikiKumakura/bulkdeconv"
url: "https://daikikumakura.github.io/software/bulkdeconv.html"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  An R package that estimates cell-type composition or abundance from human and mouse tumor bulk RNA-seq through one function, bulkdeconv(data, expr, species, method). It provides 18 published methods; 15 are implemented in the package and run after installation, and 3 use their upstream packages. Each method reports its scores, metadata and quality-control information, and the interpretation of the scores depends on the method.
keywords:
  - "RNA-seq"
  - "cell-type deconvolution"
  - "tumor microenvironment"
  - "immune infiltration"
  - "R package"
